## Common Borrow Patterns

### Read-Only Access Pattern

```xiom
type Person = { name: Str; age: Int; }

fn describe(p: &Person) {
  io.println(p.name + " is " + p.age + " years old.");
}
```

### Mutation Pattern

```xiom
fn birthday(p: &mut Person) {
  p.age = p.age + 1;  // Happy birthday!
}
```

### Read Then Write (Scoped)

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  var person = Person{ name: "Alice", age: 29 };

  describe(&person);      // Read borrow — OK
  birthday(&mut person);  // Write borrow — previous read ended, OK
  describe(&person);      // Read borrow — previous write ended, OK

  return person.age;
}
```

### Mixed Access Patterns

```xiom
fn print_and_clear(items: &mut Vec[Str]) {
  for item in &items {       // Read-like iteration
    io.println(item);
  }
  while items.len() > 0 {   // Write: clear items
    items.pop();
  }
}
```

The compiler ensures these patterns are safe by tracking exactly when each borrow starts and ends.

